MKL libary
==========

See README.oneAPI on how to obtain the MKL library.

See also the website
  https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/tools/oneapi/onemkl-link-line-advisor.html
for further advise on compile options.


In the following MKLPATH is the directory for the libraries. For Linux this
should usually be set to
   MKLPATH = $(MKLROOT)/lib/intel64
but for some systems it might not be needed at all (mac).


By default tfem is set to 4-byte integers with multi-threading:

# 4-byte integer, multi-threading for MKL
LIBBLAS = -L$(MKLPATH) -lmkl_intel_lp64 -lmkl_intel_thread -lmkl_core -liomp5 \
          -lpthread

Note, that you can also set the environment variable OMP_NUM_THREADS to the
number of threads you need. If not, the number of threads is taken equal to
the number of cores. Note also, that in order to use the pardiso solver in
MKL multi-threading is required.


If the size of real(dp) arrays become larger than 16GB, 8-byte integers are
needed. Change the lp64 library to ilp64 library:

# 64bit CPU, 8-byte integer, multi-threading for MKL
LIBBLAS = -L$(MKLPATH) -lmkl_intel_ilp64 -lmkl_intel_thread -lmkl_core -liomp5 \
          -lpthread

Note, that the compiler option for 8-byte integers needs to be set as well, 
for example -i8 for the ifx compiler and -fdefault-integer-8 for the
gfortran compiler.
